BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 405.72 Tm (Database design offers different isolation and operating burdens rather than one universally preferred layout. Software) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 390.50 Tm (Developer Diaries presents three arrangements: shared tables carrying tenant IDs, separate schemas inside one) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 375.27 Tm (database, and separate databases behind a common API. Shared tables simplify deployment, migration, and backup, but) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 360.05 Tm (a backup or restore concerns the database rather than an individual tenant. Separate schemas provide namespacing,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 344.82 Tm (easier per-tenant backup, and customization, while multiplying migration work and introducing schema-management) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 329.60 Tm (costs. Separate databases offer stronger isolation and tenant-specific scaling, with more expense and more databases to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 314.37 Tm (maintain. CodeOpinion extends the menu with mixed application and database pools: tenants A and B can share one) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 299.15 Tm (pool while tenant C occupies another, allowing changes to roll out progressively. For that hybrid arrangement,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 283.92 Tm (CodeOpinion recommends globally unique identifiers so moving tenants between databases does not create ID) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 268.70 Tm (collisions. Both speakers discuss tenant-level resource controls; CodeOpinion adds that rate limits do not eliminate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 253.47 Tm (every noisy-neighbor problem because an individual expensive query can still consume database resources. The choice) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 238.25 Tm (turns on tenant count, workload, data volume, infrastructure cost, and deployment complexity in their accounts.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 223.02 Tm (Software Developer Diaries [wrVKnQvDJy0 @ 00:09:56]; CodeOpinion [YaSPB2uNLYg @ 00:05:31].) Tj ET
