BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Recurring revenue starts with a service customers keep paying to use, not with a large invoice or a software launch.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (Dan Martell describes the customer proposition as monthly access, remote hosting, Internet accessibility, scalability,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (and regular updates. The customer avoids buying and maintaining the hardware and receives improvements through the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (subscription [UEHdYNXiIUU @ 00:06:11]. The Startup CFO turns that proposition into a measurement rule: count the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (recurring monthly equivalent, not whatever happened to be invoiced. A ?12,000 annual subscription contributes ?1,000) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (of MRR, rather than ?12,000 in January; consulting and other nonrecurring work stay outside that recurring figure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm ([Y6tSBvQhyak @ 00:18:19]. ChartMogul makes the same separation with a $1,200 annual payment: the cash arrives) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (upfront, but its MRR contribution is $100. Its operating definition asks what the existing subscriber base would pay) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (next month if nobody canceled, upgraded, or downgraded [zo3QHrXiprs @ 00:00:40]. CodeLucky starts with an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (equally concrete example: 100 customers paying $99 produce $9,900 MRR [hyC9WOKzUMc @ 00:00:54]. These) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (explanations agree on the baseline: identify the active subscription relationship and its monthly recurring value before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (discussing growth. Annual cash, one-time work, and the monthly subscription base are different views of the business,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (not interchangeable revenue trophies.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (The next shared move is to break the headline into causes. Vickery Finance opens with two businesses that both report) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm ($20,000 MRR: one has a loyal base and gentle growth, while the other churns furiously and sprints to stand still. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (number alone does not distinguish them [-XgJLhATOGI @ 00:00:00]. The Startup CFO makes the same point through) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (the monthly bridge: previous MRR plus new business, reactivation, and expansion, minus contraction and churn. Large) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (new sales alongside large losses can disguise a product customers do not keep [Y6tSBvQhyak @ 00:22:23]. Retention) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (then determines how much acquisition remains in the business. The Startup Club by Slidebean models 100 new) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (customers each month with 20% monthly churn: growth eventually stalls because the business loses about as many) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (customers as it adds. Slidebean explicitly says revenue flatlining happened to its own business [s8_Vax8VUmM @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (00:03:38]. Hustle Audit describes the same ceiling in revenue terms: new recurring revenue added each month divided) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (by monthly churn, with losses rising as the base gets larger [e-GPBm2gRsA @ 00:02:44]. The shared operating) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (question is not simply whether new customers arrived. It is how much recurring business survived, what existing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (customers changed, and whether acquisition is expanding the base or merely replacing departures.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (Customer counts and customer dollars need separate readings. At Web Summit, the speaker illustrates two accounts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (paying $1,000 and $5,000 monthly: losing either means 50% customer churn, but the revenue damage is radically) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (different. Expanding the larger account can instead offset the smaller account's departure [5RR6M_d6eKc @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm (00:13:02]. VCPete similarly describes remaining customers buying additional users or features, turning lost logos into a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm (growing revenue relationship; its example ultimately identifies 108% net revenue retention [XaOgak-YulM @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.25 Tm (00:02:45]. Revenue quality also depends on what those relationships cost. Eric Andrews defines unit economics around) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 244.02 Tm (one customer's monthly revenue, direct costs, marketing costs, lifetime profit, and the point at which the relationship) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.80 Tm (breaks even [8eHInIdNfa0 @ 00:01:21]. One Minute Finance stresses the timing problem behind that calculation: sales) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 213.57 Tm (and marketing are paid upfront while subscription receipts return in small monthly installments, so rapid sales growth) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 198.35 Tm (can drain cash [Xpw9vNbYna0 @ 00:01:19]. Together, these accounts put recurring revenue inside an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 183.12 Tm (acquisition-and-retention engine rather than outside ordinary operating work. Track the customers that remain, the) Tj ET
